rs = countLiveNeighbors(liveSet, x, y);\n    const isAlive = liveSet.has(key);\n    if (isAlive && (liveNeighbors === 2 || liveNeighbors === 3)) {\n      result.push([x, y]);\n    } else if (!isAlive && liveNeighbors === 3) {\n      result.push([x, y]);\n    }\n  }\n  return result;\n}\n```\n- Bindings: cells, liveSet, x(y in map), candidateSet, x(y in outer loop), dx(dy in inner loop), neighborKey, result, key, x(y from fromKey), liveNeighbors, isAlive = 13\n- Constants: 2, 3 = 2\n- Invocations: Set, map, toKey, Set, add, toKey, for-of iterator, add, for-of iterator, fromKey, countLiveNeighbors, has, push, push = ... let me count more carefully\n  - `new Set(...)` - invocation\n  - `cells.map(...)` - invocation\n  - `toKey(x, y)` - invocation\n  - `new Set<string>()` - invocation\n  - `candidateSet.add(toKey(x, y))` - 2 invocations (add, toKey)\n  - for-of outer - invocation (iterator)\n  - `toKey(x + dx, y + dy)` - invocation\n  - `candidateSet.add(neighborKey)` - invocation\n  - for-of inner - invocation (iterator)\n  - for-of result loop - invocation (iterator)\n  - `fromKey(key)` - invocation\n  - `countLiveNeighbors(liveSet, x, y)` - invocation\n  - `liveSet.has(key)` - invocation\n  - `result.push([x, y])` - invocation (appears twice)\n  Total: 14 invocations\n- Conditionals: if, else if = 2\n- Loops: for-of outer, for-of inner, for-of result = 3\n- Assignments: liveSet, candidateSet, neighborKey, result, x/y fromKey destructure, liveNeighbors, isAlive = 7\n\nMass: 13*1 + 2*1 + 14*2 + 2*4 + 3*5 + 7*6 = 13 + 2 + 28 + 8 + 15 + 42 = 108\n\n**Total Current Mass: 0 + 3 + 16 + 22 + 34 + 108 = 183**\n\nNow for the refactored code:\n\nChanges:\n1. `liveNeighbors` → `liveNeighborCount` (no mass change, just a name)\n2. Remove `neighborKey` variable, inline `toKey(x + dx, y + dy)` into `candidateSet.add()`\n3. Merge if/else into single condition\n\nAfter change 2:\n- Bindings: -1 (no neighborKey)\n- Invocations: same (add and toKey still called)\n- Assignments: -1 (no 